                <pb facs="0699" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.13/128: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-14T15:00:00-05:00">November 14, 1919—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 15—12:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3762. For Polk. Your 5123, November 11, 9 p.m. It has been found impossible to
                    have U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">George Washington</hi> make another trip,
                    but the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">America</hi> operated by the War
                    Department will be at Brest on or about December 1st. Arrangements will be made
                    with the War Department for shipping all Mission files, documents, etc., on the
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">America</hi> if you so desire.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
